ws:","context":"Fair value of financial instruments","section":"Segment reporting","block":139,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-043473","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-21","reportDate":"2026-09-21","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226043473/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c.bin","sha256":"24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c"}},{"id":"e5c0560904d9ffde5e3173b09fb75fb91b4a471eaf28b8aa7b99fe123d10dcf1","quote":"Level 1 – Quoted prices in active markets for identical assets and liabilities.","context":"The fair value of a financial instrument is defined as the exchange price that would be received from an asset or paid to transfer a liability (as exit price) in the principal or most advantageous market for the asset or liability in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date. A three-level fair value hierarchy prioritizes the inputs used to measure fair value. The hierarchy requires entities to maximize the use of observable inputs and minimize the use of unobservable inputs. The three levels of inputs used to measure fair value are as follows:","section":"Segment reporting","block":140,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-043473","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-21","reportDate":"2026-09-21","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226043473/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c.bin","sha256":"24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c"}},{"id":"858bb0db99ca31cdc4e3c70fc7f026fd93ccecf3339a32710b19c1fc39e7a6fb","quote":"Level 2 – Quoted prices in active markets for similar assets and liabilities, or other inputs that are observable for the asset or liability, either directly or indirectly, for substantially the full term of the financial instrument.","context":"Level 1 – Quoted prices in active markets for identical assets and liabilities.","section":"Segment reporting","block":141,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-043473","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-21","reportDate":"2026-09-21","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226043473/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c.bin","sha256":"24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c"}},{"id":"08c8bdf88d47c42f74a35cce9a5392cce64b4e6b0236fea6b13278e6711f78c7","quote":"Level 3 – Unobservable inputs that are supported by little or no market activity and that are significant to the fair value of the assets and liabilities. This includes certain pricing models, discounted cash flow methodologies and similar techniques that use significant unobservable inputs.","context":"Level 2 – Quoted prices in active markets for similar assets and liabilities, or other inputs that are observable for the asset or liability, either directly or indirectly, for substantially the full term of the financial instrument.","section":"Segment reporting","block":142,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-043473","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-21","reportDate":"2026-09-21","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226043473/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c.bin","sha256":"24fe08ed5576a454376a6f04f6265114fadcc6bf7bf0916a9ad42c55a9db2c3c"}},{"id":"1d8da73f7206ed525a48a1924f01097514