d from an asset or paid to transfer a liability (as exit price) in the principal or most advantageous market for the asset or liability in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date. A three-level fair value hierarchy prioritizes the inputs used to measure fair value. The hierarchy requires entities to maximize the use of observable inputs and minimize the use of unobservable inputs. The three levels of inputs used to measure fair value are as follows:","section":"Segment reporting","block":128,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-043473","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-21","reportDate":"2026-09-21","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226043473/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b69fa2012cbd01c930db7bed8a7a5c6c1c7b61107dad97e01b5a5923f7d450e5.bin","sha256":"b69fa2012cbd01c930db7bed8a7a5c6c1c7b61107dad97e01b5a5923f7d450e5"}},{"id":"6badeba6425d70bcbc1dd4fa0049c8c0e9d82cc41b695e8a83d1be1560ebf040","quote":"Level 2 – Quoted prices in active markets for similar assets and liabilities, or other inputs that are observable for the asset or liability, either directly or indirectly, for substantially the full term of the financial instrument.","context":"Level 1 – Quoted prices in active markets for identical assets and liabilities.","section":"Segment reporting","block":129,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-043473","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-21","reportDate":"2026-09-21","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226043473/ex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b69fa2012cbd01c930db7bed8a7a5c6c1c7b61107dad97e01b5a5923f7d450e5.bin","sha256":"b69fa2012cbd01c930db7bed8a7a5c6c1c7b61107dad97e01b5a5923f7d450e5"}},{"id":"58649a29d93b9241190dcaa685393c494670